stealth: belt-and-suspenders hook on the GC report emitter

Adds a second layer to the 20-hour cooldown defeat. Even if our byte
write loses the race for a frame, the only function that actually sends
Game::ChatReportError("#SFUI_QMM_ERROR_X_InsecureBlocked") to Steam GC
is now hooked to early-return.

Reversed via IDA:
  - sub_180C4A6C0 = the lone emitter. Decompile shows:
      KeyValues("Game::ChatReportError") -> SetString(error,
        "#SFUI_QMM_ERROR_X_InsecureBlocked") -> dispatch via
        qword_18253FAA0+24 (matchmaking session manager).
      Then fires "OnClientInsecureBlocked" UI event.
  - Only one direct code xref: from sub_180F23200 (per-tick reader).
    Three data xrefs are vtables that route via reason strings
    "init", "init_cmd", "init_tools". Hooking the entry catches all.
  - Confirmed sub_180F1F830 (start-listen-server reader) does NOT
    call sub_180C4A6C0 -- has its own local UI/disconnect path with
    no GC report. So zeroing the byte already neutralizes that one.

Implementation:
  - stealth.h: InsecureEmitter_Detour(const char*) { return 0; }
    + state vars: g_pInsecureEmitterAddr / Tramp / Tried / Ok.
  - dllmain.cpp main loop: lazy sigscan
      "48 89 5C 24 20 56 48 83 EC 20 48 8B D9 48 89 6C 24 30
       48 8B E9 48 8B 0D ? ? ? ? 48 8B 01"
    (verified UNIQUE in client.dll @ 14152), MH_CreateHook +
    MH_EnableHook once. All callers of the original discard its
    return value, so returning 0 is behaviorally invisible.

Watermark:
  - Adds a "GC" badge after the byte value: GREEN = hook installed,
    GRAY = pending, AMBER = pattern miss / MinHook failed.

Cost: one extra MinHook trampoline. No additional runtime overhead --
the detour is never even reached when the byte stays at 0.
